    "title": "Donald V. Beauregard",
    "text": "Donald “Don” V. Beauregard, 82, a resident of Jamestown, R.I., for more than 20 years, passed away peacefully at home Friday, Oct. 31, 2025.\nHe was the beloved husband of Sandra “Sandy” J. (Anderson) Beauregard.\nBorn in Central Falls, Don was the son of the late Victor and Georgette (Tremblay) Beauregard.\nA lifelong resident of Rhode Island, aside from four years spent in Chicago, Don was a proud graduate of Sacred Heart Academy, Class of 1961. He went on to earn a Bachelor of Science degree in physics from Providence College in 1965 and a Master of Science degree in physics in 1967.\nDon was a dedicated scientist and inventor who spent much of his career in private industry before retiring from the Naval Undersea Warfare Center (NUWC) after 30 years of distinguished federal service.\nA former member of the East Greenwich Yacht Club, Don loved spending time on the water aboard his sailboat, Seraphin. He also found joy in music, gardening and cars. Don and his wife, Sandy, shared a love of travel, exploring much of the United States and Europe together throughout the years.\nHe was the loving father of Bradford Beauregard (wife, Deanne) and the late John Beauregard; step-father of Deborah Johnson (husband, Darryl), and Laurie Goodman. Don also is survived by seven grandchildren.\nFuneral services will be held privately at the convenience of the family.\nKindly visit the Fagan-Quinn Funeral Home online for memorial tributes and additional information, www.PatrickQuinnFuneralsandCremations.com.",
